@* DS parity — no consumer yet. The rail list is the design system's ALTERNATIVE rendering
   of an effective-dated record table, and both candidates — account terms and account
   estimates — render their history as a table today (the estimates timeline's per-surface
   CSS was never mounted either). Built here so the atom exists once rather than being
   re-derived per surface the first time one of them offers the switch. *@
@*
    OdsTimeline — the vertical rail history list (Odyssey Design System · components/Timeline).

    The alternative rendering of any effective-dated record table — terms, estimates,
    renewals. A plain rail container; the rows are <OdsTimelineItem> children, newest
    first. The rail segment is drawn by each item, so the list needs no wrapper line and
    the last item ends the rail cleanly whatever the count.
*@

<div class="odc-timeline @Class" @attributes="UserAttributes">
    @ChildContent
</div>

@code {
    /// <summary><see cref="OdsTimelineItem"/> children, newest first.</summary>
    [Parameter] public RenderFragment? ChildContent { get; set; }

    /// <summary>Extra CSS class(es) appended to the root.</summary>
    [Parameter] public string? Class { get; set; }

    [Parameter(CaptureUnmatchedValues = true)]
    public Dictionary<string, object>? UserAttributes { get; set; }
}
